Subject: text-shimmer-v2: the peak copy aligns its glyphs to the left of its box

What: the peak copy sets text-align: left.
Why: the peak box is as wide as the sweep, so an inherited text-align: center (a button) pushed its glyphs past the swept copy's clip and the band painted nothing.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css b/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css
index 6063ab8d6e..060b60158b 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css
@@ -93,9 +93,13 @@
   animation-name: text-shimmer-v2-sweep;
 }
 
+/* The peak's box is as wide as the sweep, and its offset assumes its glyphs sit at the
+   box's left edge. An inherited text-align (a <button> centres) would move them past the
+   swept copy's clip, and the band would paint nothing. */
 [data-component="text-shimmer-v2"] .ui-text-shimmer-v2-peak {
   display: block;
   white-space: pre;
+  text-align: left;
   background-image: var(--_peak);
   -webkit-background-clip: text;
   background-clip: text;
